# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule, evaluating the GNOF
# (Piris natural orbital functional, Occ_opt/PNOFs.h) RDMFT functional
# -- the PNOF counterpart of water_muller.inp's own JK-only MULLER run.
# FUNCTIONAL does not need DEBUG -- setting it (as here) makes main.cpp
# build the PNOF orbital subspaces (Occ_opt/Orb_subspaces.h;
# PNOF_SUBSPACES 1 by default: just the HOMO subspace) with
# PNOF_COUPLING 2 (HOMO coupled with LUMO alone), give each subspace a
# feasible initial guess (principal near 1, its virtual near 0), and
# then OPTIMIZE the geminal occupations at those same fixed orbitals
# via Occ_opt/SQP.h subject to sum(n) = 1 per subspace -- all printed
# right after each "Total ... energy" line. With NO FUNCTIONAL keyword
# at all (see water.inp), this whole step is skipped entirely.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_COUPLING 2

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
